  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral support for priority collective sites, providing individual support to the most vulnerable cases and implementing education catch-up program in the Western part of Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtBased on the needs assessment, Key informant interviews&#xa0;with beneficiaries, community leaders who are aware of the problems of IDPs living in collective sites in Ternopil, Chernivtsi, Zakarpattia, Ivano-Frankivsk and Khmelnytskyi regions, as well as those who are aware of the gaps in education of displaced, non-displaced and returned children in Rivne and Volyn regions, it was decided to provide multisectoral support for priority collective sites, providing individual support to the most vulnerable cases&#xa0; and implementing education catch-up program in the Western part of UkraineltbrgtThe general idea of the project is to help various vulnerable categories in the most convenient way for them, to cover the most common needs. Several areas of activity were identified. Firstly, coordinated multi-sectoral interventions to bring prioritized collective sites in line with minimum humanitarian standards as per Resolution 930 &#x2018;On collective site functioning&#x2019; and provide critical individual assistance for the most vulnerable IDPs in collective sites. Secondly, catch-up learning will be organized in a structured way to provide access displaced, non-displaced and returnee children, considering gender, age, and inclusivity approaches to enable appropriate socializing process and shape groups of interest for different age-appropriate thematics.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
